---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Corrections Policy | Micro Signal Cosmos"
  description="Corrections Policy for Micro Signal Cosmos. Read our transparent procedures for identifying, reviewing, correcting, and logging editorial errors."
  canonical="https://microsignalcosmos.com/corrections-policy/"
>
  <Header />

  <main id="main-content" class="bg-[#F7F9FC] py-12 sm:py-20">
    <div class="container-main">

      <!-- Breadcrumbs -->
      <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="mb-8">
        <ol class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-[#697586]">
          <li>
            <a href="/" class="transition-colors hover:text-[#14233B]">Home</a>
          </li>
          <li aria-hidden="true" class="text-slate-300">/</li>
          <li aria-current="page" class="font-medium text-[#14233B]">Corrections Policy</li>
        </ol>
      </nav>

      <!-- Header Section -->
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl text-center">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-[#E3E8EF] bg-white px-3.5 py-1.5 shadow-xs">
          <span class="h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-[#3478F6]"></span>
          <span class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-wider text-[#14233B] uppercase">
            Editorial Accountability
          </span>
        </div>

        <h1 class="mt-6 text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-[#14233B] sm:text-5xl">
          Corrections <span class="text-[#3478F6]">Policy</span>
        </h1>

        <p class="mt-4 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-[#697586]">
          Effective Date: November 2026 &bull; Micro Signal Cosmos Editorial Desk
        </p>

        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[#4B5565] sm:text-lg">
          Our transparent framework for admitting, rectifying, and documenting errors openly and promptly across all published articles.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Main Document -->
      <article class="mx-auto mt-12 max-w-3xl rounded-2xl border border-[#E3E8EF] bg-white p-8 sm:p-12 shadow-sm text-sm leading-relaxed text-[#4B5565] space-y-10">

        <!-- 1. The Accountability Principle -->
        <section aria-labelledby="accountability-principle">
          <h2 id="accountability-principle" class="text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-[#14233B]">
            1. The Accountability Principle
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            At <strong class="font-semibold text-[#14233B]">Micro Signal Cosmos</strong>, our pursuit of journalistic precision does not mean we are immune to error. When an inaccuracy, misattribution, or technical misstatement occurs, we believe that candid, transparent correction is the highest demonstration of editorial integrity.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We do not silently alter past coverage, erase problematic statements without notice, or pretend mistakes never happened. Substantive changes are always marked, explained, and dated for our readers.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- 2. Categorization of Editorial Updates -->
        <section aria-labelledby="update-categories" class="border-t border-[#E3E8EF] pt-8">
          <h2 id="update-categories" class="text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-[#14233B]">
            2. Categorization of Editorial Updates
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We classify updates to published material into three clear categories:
          </p>

          <div class="mt-6 space-y-4">
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-rose-200 bg-rose-50/50 p-5">
              <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-rose-700">Category A</span>
              <h3 class="mt-1 text-sm font-bold text-[#14233B]">Substantive Factual Corrections</h3>
              <p class="mt-2 text-xs leading-relaxed text-[#4B5565]">
                Applied when an article contains a factual error—such as an incorrect measurement unit, mistaken scientific attribution, erroneous timeline, or flawed mathematical formulation. A visible <em>"Correction Notice"</em> is appended to the bottom or top of the article noting the exact date of revision and clarifying what was changed.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="rounded-xl border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50/50 p-5">
              <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-amber-700">Category B</span>
              <h3 class="mt-1 text-sm font-bold text-[#14233B]">Clarifications & Context Additions</h3>
              <p class="mt-2 text-xs leading-relaxed text-[#4B5565]">
                Applied when an explanation was technically accurate but open to misunderstanding or missing crucial context (such as an updated experimental replication result). A <em>"Clarification Note"</em> is placed on the article explaining the supplementary nuance.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="rounded-xl border border-[#E3E8EF] bg-[#F7F9FC] p-5">
              <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#697586]">Category C</span>
              <h3 class="mt-1 text-sm font-bold text-[#14233B]">Minor Typographical Adjustments</h3>
              <p class="mt-2 text-xs leading-relaxed text-[#697586]">
                Grammar corrections, broken link repairs, and minor spelling fixes that do not alter the factual meaning of the reporting are corrected directly in the source file without requiring a formal notice.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 3. How Readers Can Submit a Correction Request -->
        <section aria-labelledby="submitting-corrections" class="border-t border-[#E3E8EF] pt-8">
          <h2 id="submitting-corrections" class="text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-[#14233B]">
            3. How to Submit a Correction Request
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            If you believe you have detected an inaccuracy in any published Micro Signal Cosmos dispatch, please notify us directly:
          </p>
          <div class="mt-4 rounded-xl border border-[#E3E8EF] bg-white p-6 shadow-xs">
            <h4 class="text-sm font-bold text-[#14233B]">Correction Submission Guidelines</h4>
            <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-xs text-[#4B5565]">
              <li><strong class="font-semibold text-[#14233B]">Target URL:</strong> Provide the exact link to the article in question.</li>
              <li><strong class="font-semibold text-[#14233B]">Exact Text:</strong> Quote the sentence or section containing the alleged error.</li>
              <li><strong class="font-semibold text-[#14233B]">Supporting Evidence:</strong> Provide a direct hyperlink to primary evidence (e.g. peer-reviewed journal DOI, official GitHub commit, manufacturer documentation).</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="mt-6">
              <a
                href="/contact/"
                class="inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-[#3478F6] px-4 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-white transition-colors hover:bg-[#2563EB]"
              >
                Submit Correction via Contact Form &rarr;
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 4. Retraction Policy -->
        <section aria-labelledby="retraction-policy" class="border-t border-[#E3E8EF] pt-8">
          <h2 id="retraction-policy" class="text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-[#14233B]">
            4. Article Retraction Protocols
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            In rare cases where an underlying academic study is retracted by its publisher, or if an article is found to have breached foundational editorial ethics, a formal retraction is executed.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Rather than deleting the webpage and producing a dead 404 URL, the article URL remains active with a prominent header explaining why the piece was retracted. This maintains historical transparency and digital accountability for our archive.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Related Standards Navigation -->
        <section class="border-t border-[#E3E8EF] pt-8">
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-[#14233B]">Related Governance Standards</h3>
          <div class="mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3">
            <a href="/editorial-policy/" class="rounded-lg border border-[#E3E8EF] bg-[#F7F9FC] p-3 text-xs font-semibold text-[#14233B] transition-colors hover:border-[#3478F6] hover:text-[#3478F6]">
              Editorial Policy &rarr;
            </a>
            <a href="/fact-checking-policy/" class="rounded-lg border border-[#E3E8EF] bg-[#F7F9FC] p-3 text-xs font-semibold text-[#14233B] transition-colors hover:border-[#3478F6] hover:text-[#3478F6]">
              Fact-checking Standards &rarr;
            </a>
            <a href="/about/" class="rounded-lg border border-[#E3E8EF] bg-[#F7F9FC] p-3 text-xs font-semibold text-[#14233B] transition-colors hover:border-[#3478F6] hover:text-[#3478F6]">
              About the Publication &rarr;
            </a>
          </div>
        </section>

      </article>

    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

